  "description": "All entry points require UDP recon. TCP scans show nothing useful. SNMP, TFTP, DNS zone transfer are the keys. AD: MS01 (SNMP → creds → WinRM), MS02 (TFTP → config → creds), DC01. Standalone: BOX1 (DNS zone transfer → hidden subdomain), BOX2 (SNMP → service discovery), BOX3 (UDP service on high port).",

  "introduction": "When TCP is quiet, UDP holds the keys—SNMP, TFTP, DNS. This scenario trains you to enumerate UDP and find hidden entry points.",
  "mental_model": "Think: TCP empty = try UDP. SNMP leaks creds; TFTP has configs; DNS zone transfer reveals hidden hosts.",
  "key_principles": [
    "nmap -sU for UDP when TCP shows nothing",
    "snmpwalk with public/private community",
    "TFTP get for config files",
    "dig axfr for zone transfer",
    "UDP high ports may have custom services"
  ],

